<h2 class="mt-14">Consent and purchaser suppression for Customer lifecycle</h2>
<p>Before launching customer lifecycle automation, prove every app in the stack logs email and SMS consent auditably, with purchase events cutting promotional follow-up the moment checkout completes. Customer Lifecycle audiences forgive plain creative; they do not forgive promos sent mid-refund or right after checkout.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Suppress customer lifecycle marketing entirely until consent is documented</td><td>Customer Lifecycle consent is the legal basis of every send</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Open customer lifecycle with guidance and proof, not discounts</td><td>Customer Lifecycle margin suffers when discounts arrive first</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Context-rich customer lifecycle nudge before any incentive</td><td>Protects customer lifecycle profit when purchase intent is hottest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Recent customer lifecycle buyers exit promos into onboarding</td><td>Keeps customer lifecycle buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>Hold customer lifecycle marketing while service cases stay open</td><td>Service-active customer lifecycle shoppers reject promos</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Customer Lifecycle sunset policy precedes complaint spikes</td><td>Keeps customer lifecycle placement high via list hygiene</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Customer Lifecycle texting respects time and frequency rules</td><td>Text grievances hit customer lifecycle programs hardest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Isolate customer lifecycle wholesale comms from retail blasts</td><td>B2B customer lifecycle mis-sends risk contract breach</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Customer Lifecycle automation skips unverified domains first</td><td>Customer Lifecycle bounces from junk signups hurt inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Strip customer lifecycle test data from live journeys</td><td>Customer Lifecycle test sends skew attribution reads</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>No bespoke customer lifecycle track for competitor signals</td><td>Manual customer lifecycle exceptions rot the audit trail</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Reconfirm customer lifecycle consent where timestamps are missing</td><td>Customer Lifecycle lists without proof invite liability</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Margin, app costs, and pricing for Customer lifecycle</h2>
<p>Attributed revenue is not profit for customer lifecycle. A self-funding customer lifecycle program survives a full cost model: subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, capture tooling, templates, agency time, and every point of customer lifecycle discount margin. When the customer lifecycle stack nears fifteen percent of email-attributed margin, simplify the customer lifecycle setup before tuning it.</p>
<p>Pricing changes frequently and varies by region, contact volume, and contract term, so check the official pricing pages of every shortlisted app and model an eighteen-month total that includes a peak season. For customer lifecycle, free plans always bind somewhere; identify whether contacts, sends, branching, or support caps your customer lifecycle motion first.</p>
